From 21af89fdaf79790ab0b15b29cd551f4a9e9ffdc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:37:09 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Measured geometry is trusted; a wrong posted size is kept,
 not assumed

Unevenly split files had their measured, exact sizes stored untrusted, so stream
reads checked no offset or length and a wrong article under a segment's id was
served. A file whose =ybegin size= is wrong (disproved by its last part or PAR2)
was trusted but checked against its decoded size, so every article was refused.
Segments now keep the posted size when it differs (blob version 5).
